From b888be8f1880591934f8e914fd256c22587a5608 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mi210 <mi210@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:19:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] hip: Inkling-2 single-token GEMVs (NVFP4 MoE, BF16) +
 faster mix

- NVFP4 MUL_MAT_ID (one token): 8 lanes per row, 256-thread blocks,
  q8_1 activations staged in LDS, int8 dot products as mul_mat_vec_q,
  exact bit-built UE4M3 decode (the gfx90a fallback used ldexpf + div),
  per-expert scale (RESHAPE/REPEAT/GET_ROWS/MUL) fused. ~1.3 TB/s.
- BF16 MUL_MAT (one token): 16-byte loads, 32/64/256 lanes per row by
  row count; GEMVs sharing the activation are merged into one launch
  (later ones computed early, guarded by the buffer-reuse check).
  q/gate/o ~1.2 TB/s, LM head ~1.4 TB/s.
- mix: single 1024-thread block, all states loaded at once, the same
  two-level rms reduction tree (bit-identical), normalized states in LDS,
  contiguous transposed writes; S <= 5 templated (no scratch).
Switches GGML_CUDA_INK_NVFP4/_BF16/_BF16_MERGE=0. tg128 44.8 -> 50.7
tok/s; KLD vs baseline 0.00079 (top-1 99.87%), the GEMV summation-order
noise floor; with the GEMVs off logits stay bit-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
